I'll write this as a fast byte-buffer program.

Design:
- The LCG uses integer arithmetic: seed = (seed*3877 + 29573) % 139968. The maximum seed*3877 is about 5.4e8, which fits in an int.
- For symbol selection, r = seed/139968.0, and the first symbol whose cumulative probability is strictly greater than r is chosen. To keep this exact, I compute the comparison in double the same way as the reference: cumulative sums accumulated in double, compared against seed/139968.0. A lookup table is the fast route: precompute for each of the 139968 possible seed values the symbol index, using the exact double comparison. The table costs 140k entries times a short linear scan, which is cheap.
- If no cumulative probability exceeds r because of rounding (the final cumulative sum is about 0.99999999 and r is at most 0.99999286), pick the last symbol. This is safe here: the largest r is 139967/139968 ≈ 0.9999929, and the final cumulative sum is ≈ 1.0.
- Output goes into a byte buffer that is flushed to System.out when full. Each sequence is written with a newline after every 60 characters and a final newline if the last line is partial.
- Section 1: the sequence is the ALU string repeated cyclically, length 2N, with index k running over the ALU string (wrapping at 287).
- Section 2 and 3: each character comes from the table lookup. The seed carries over between the two sections.

Implementation of the writer: keep a byte[] buf of 1<<16 and a position, and flush with System.out.write(buf, 0, pos) through a BufferedOutputStream or FileOutputStream. A column counter handles the line wrapping.

For the cumulative probabilities, the table for section 2 is built in order, adding the probabilities in double. A symbol is chosen at the first i where cum[i] > r.

Lengths are up to 5N = 125M for N=25M, so I use long for the counters.

```java
import java.io.*;

public class fasta {
    static byte[] buf = new byte[1 << 16];
    static int pos = 0;
    static OutputStream out;

    static void flush() throws IOException {
        out.write(buf, 0, pos);
        pos = 0;
    }

    static byte[] buildLookup(byte[] syms, double[] probs) {
        int n = syms.length;
        double[] cum = new double[n];
        double c = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            c += probs[i];
            cum[i] = c;
        }
        byte[] t = new byte[139968];
        for (int s = 0; s < 139968; s++) {
            double r = s / 139968.0;
            int k = n - 1;
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                if (cum[i] > r) {
                    k = i;
                    break;
                }
            }
            t[s] = syms[k];
        }
        return t;
    }

    static int seed = 42;

    static void random(byte[] table, long len) throws IOException {
        int col = 0;
        int sd = seed;
        for (long i = 0; i < len; i++) {
            sd = (sd * 3877 + 29573) % 139968;
            if (pos + 2 > buf.length) flush();
            buf[pos++] = table[sd];
            if (++col == 60) {
                buf[pos++] = '\n';
                col = 0;
            }
        }
        if (col != 0) {
            if (pos + 1 > buf.length) flush();
            buf[pos++] = '\n';
        }
        seed = sd;
    }

    static void header(String s) throws IOException {
        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
            if (pos + 2 > buf.length) flush();
            buf[pos++] = (byte) s.charAt(i);
        }
        buf[pos++] = '\n';
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
        long n = Long.parseLong(args[0]);
        out = new FileOutputStream(FileDescriptor.out);
        String alu = "GGCCGGGCGCGGTGGCTCACGCCTGTAATCCCAGCACTTTGGGAGGCCGAGGCGGGCGGA"
                + "TCACCTGAGGTCAGGAGTTCGAGACCAGCCTGGCCAACATGGTGAAACCCCGTCTCTACT"
                + "AAAAATACAAAAATTAGCCGGGCGTGGTGGCGCGCGCCTGTAATCCCAGCTACTCGGGAG"
                + "GCTGAGGCAGGAGAATCGCTTGAACCCGGGAGGCGGAGGTTGCAGTGAGCCGAGATCGCG"

